#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:67
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "&kappname; is a fun and exciting game for &kde; desktop environment. &kappname; is modeled after the well known pen and paper based game of Dots and Boxes."
msgid "&ksquares; is a fun and exciting game by &kde;. &ksquares; is modeled after the well known pen and paper based game of Dots and Boxes."
msgstr "O &kappname; é un xogo divertido e emocionante para o entorno de escritorio &kde;. O &kappname; baséase no famoso xogo de papel e bolígrafo dos Cadrados."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:68
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "The idea behind &kappname; is to construct squares by interconnecting the dots on the grid. Up to four players can play this game together, taking turns. The trick is – regardless of who has constructed most of the square, it is the player who completes the square that gets the point for it."
msgid "The idea behind &ksquares; is to construct squares by interconnecting the dots on the grid. Up to four players can play this game together, taking turns. The trick is – regardless of who has constructed most of the square, it is the player who completes the square that gets the point for it."
msgstr "A idea do &kappname; é construír cadrados conectando os puntos da cuadrícula. Poden xogar ata catro xogadores, cada un na súa quenda. O truco consiste en que non importa quen construíse a maior parte dun cadrado, é o xogador que completa o cadrado o que obtén un punto por el."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:69
#, no-c-format
msgid "To win the game round player has to collect the most points by covering the most area with the squares of player's own color."
msgstr "Para gañar unha partida hai que obter o maior número de puntos cubrindo a maior área posíbel cos cadrados da cor de cada un."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:72
#, no-c-format
msgid "How to Play"
msgstr "Como xogar"

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Objective:"
msgstr "Obxectivo:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "Complete more squares than any of your opponents."
msgstr "Completar máis cadrados que o resto dos adversarios."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid "At the start of the game, the game board is empty. There is simply a grid of dots showing where lines can be drawn."
msgstr "No inicio do xogo o taboleiro está baleiro. Simplemente hai unha grade con puntos que mostran onde se poden debuxar as liñas."

#. Tag: phrase
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:86
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "Game Board"
msgid "&ksquares; Game Board"
msgstr "Taboleiro de xogo"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:91
#, no-c-format
msgid "Each player takes it in turns to draw a line between two adjacent dots on the board. By hovering the mouse over the game board, a yellow indicator line will show you where your line will be placed when you click. Once you have decided where you want to draw your line, click - and the line will be drawn. If by drawing a line, you completed a square then this square now belongs to you and earns you a point. Each time you complete a square, you must draw another line. If your line did not complete a square then the next player(s) take their turn. The game will continue until every square on the board is owned by one of the players."
msgstr "Cada xogador debuxa unha liña entre dous puntos contiguos. Ao pasar o rato por riba do taboleiro, unha liña indicadora en amarelo mostra onde aparecería unha liña ao premer - preme e debúxase esa liña. Se ao debuxares unha liña completas un cadrado, ese cadrado perténcelle e gañas un punto. Cada vez que completes un cadrado tes que debuxar outra liña. Se a liña que debuxes non completa un cadrado, é a volta do xogador seguinte. O xogo continúa ata que todos os cadrados do taboleiro teñan dono."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:96
#, no-c-format
msgid "To start a new game with custom settings (number of players, player names, board size) click on the <guibutton>New</guibutton> toolbar button or go to <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo></shortcut><guimenu>Game</guimenu><guimenuitem>New</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. To start a new game with the same settings as the current game, click on <guibutton>Restart Game</guibutton> on the toolbar."
msgstr "Para iniciar unha partida nova con opcións personalizadas (número de xogadores, os seus nomes, o tamaño do taboleiro), preme o botón <guibutton>Nova</guibutton> da barra de ferramentas ou vai a <menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action=\"simul\">&Ctrl;<keycap>N</keycap></keycombo></shortcut><guimenu>Partida</guimenu><guimenuitem>Nova</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Para iniciar unha partida coas mesmas opcións que na que estás, preme <guibutton>Reiniciar a partida</guibutton> na barra de ferramentas."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules, Strategies and Tips"
msgstr "Regras do xogo, estratexias e suxestións"

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:104
#, no-c-format
msgid "Game Rules"
msgstr "Regras do xogo"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:105
#, fuzzy, no-c-format
#| msgid "There is very little to be said when it come to the rules, as the game concept in itself is rather a simple one. Nevertheless, here are the game regulations you, as a player will defiantly face while playing &kappname;:"
msgid "There is very little to be said when it come to the rules, as the game concept in itself is rather a simple one. Nevertheless, here are the game regulations you, as a player will defiantly face while playing &ksquares;:"
msgstr "Pouco hai que dicir no que fai ás regras, dado que o concepto do xogo é bastante sinxelo en si mesmo. Porén, velaquí as regras do xogo ás que te has de enfrontar cando xogues ao &kappname;:"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:107
#, no-c-format
msgid "You may only connect the dots on the grid if they are not previously connected by you, your opponent, or the computer."
msgstr "Só podes conectar os puntos da grade se non conectáchedes antes ti, o teu adversario ou o computador."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "To gain the points you have to connect the dots to form a square."
msgstr "Para gañar os puntos hai que conectar os puntos para formar un cadrado."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:109
#, no-c-format
msgid "The square can be no larger than the four adjacent dots on the grid allow for."
msgstr "O cadrado non pode ser maior que o que permiten os catro puntos adxacentes da grade."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:110
#, no-c-format
msgid "Once a square is complete the player who draws the last line of that square is granted the right of possession over it. The square then is colored and the player is given a point."
msgstr "Unha vez completado un cadrado, o xogador que debuxase a última liña dese cadrado recibe a súa posesión. O cadrado recibe a cor do xogador e este recibe un punto."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:111
#, no-c-format
msgid "The player who completes the square is given an extra turn which the player cannot forfeit."
msgstr "O xogador que completa o cadrado recibe unha volta extra que non pode saltar."

#. Tag: title
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:115
#, no-c-format
msgid "Strategies and Tips"
msgstr "Estratexias e suxestións"

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:117
#, no-c-format
msgid "Try not to play at random. Such game practice will most certainly result in loss."
msgstr "Intenta non xogar ao chou. Este tipo de xogo seguro que remata cunha perda."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "Construct long chains of lines over the gameboard. Once one such chain is complete start to build another one going parallel to the first."
msgstr "Constrúe cadeas longas de liñas no taboleiro. Unha vez que unha desas cadeas estea completa, comeza a construír outra que vaia paralela á primeira."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:119
#, no-c-format
msgid "Try not to build contraptions where only one line remains undone. Your opponent will almost certainly take an advantage of it."
msgstr "Intenta non construír tarecos nos que só quede unha liña desfeita. O teu opoñente aproveitarao con casi total seguranza."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:120
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you are to let the opponent get a square or more, try to select the combination resulting in the least damage."
msgstr "Se tes que permitir que o teu adversario constrúa un cadrado ou máis, intenta escoller a combinación que produza o menor dano posíbel."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid "Try to push your opponent into the situation where he/she(it) will have no choice but to let you get the square."
msgstr "Intenta empurrar o teu adversario a unha situación na que non teña máis remedio que deixarche coller o cadrado."

#. Tag: para
#. +> trunk5 stable5
#: index.docbook:122
#, no-c-format
msgid "If you are to get a chance to start completing a whole chain of squares, remember that by leaving two squares at the end of such chain incomplete you are pushing your opponent into completing them, thus giving you the opportunity to continue onto yet another chain. Such a situation is called the double-cross."
msgstr "Se tes a posibilidade de comezar a completar unha cadea completa de cadrados, lembra ao que deixares dous cadrados do final desa cadea incompletos, estás empurrando o teu adversario a completalos, dándoche así a oportunidade de continuares noutra cadea. Esta situación chámase a cruz dobre."

